1
00:00:01,584 --> 00:00:04,337
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

2
00:00:04,421 --> 00:00:07,966
["Mr. Tailor" playing]

3
00:00:08,049 --> 00:00:09,801
- <i>♪ Fix it</i> ♪
- <i>♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

4
00:00:09,884 --> 00:00:12,137
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

5
00:00:12,220 --> 00:00:15,932
♪ <i>One cut, and it's settled</i> ♪

6
00:00:16,725 --> 00:00:19,352
[Janine] Do you still
have feelings for Daddy?

7
00:00:19,436 --> 00:00:22,105
Auntie Audrey is a big check for me!

8
00:00:22,188 --> 00:00:23,523
See, you're blushing!

9
00:00:26,568 --> 00:00:28,820
- [Janine] That's the grumpy man.
- Hey! You two!

10
00:00:28,903 --> 00:00:30,405
She's the one who threw it, not me!

11
00:00:30,488 --> 00:00:31,948
[Leon] <i>You lying child, huh!</i>

12
00:00:32,032 --> 00:00:33,408
[Janine] <i>I'll tell my mommy and daddy.</i>

13
00:00:33,491 --> 00:00:34,868
<i>You're a bad person!</i>

14
00:00:34,951 --> 00:00:36,953
I didn't like what you did to my child.

15
00:00:37,037 --> 00:00:38,621
Do you think I'm afraid of you?

16
00:00:38,705 --> 00:00:40,999
[Leon] <i>That's why there are unruly kids</i>
<i>because of people like you!</i>

17
00:00:41,082 --> 00:00:42,459
- [Leon] <i>Come here!</i>
- [Audrey gasps]

18
00:00:42,542 --> 00:00:44,252
[Ibyang] <i>That man is dangerous.</i>

19
00:00:44,335 --> 00:00:45,336
<i>He has a gun!</i>

20
00:00:45,420 --> 00:00:46,880
- [gunfire]
- [Audrey screams] Atoy!

21
00:00:47,756 --> 00:00:48,715
[Audrey] Atoy!

22
00:00:48,798 --> 00:00:50,300
- [squeals]
- [gunfire]

23
00:00:50,383 --> 00:00:52,051
- Come on, drive for me!
- S-Sorry.

24
00:00:52,135 --> 00:00:53,803
I don't have the keys to my car.

25
00:00:53,887 --> 00:00:55,430
- You're useless!
- [shrieks]

26
00:00:55,513 --> 00:00:57,640
- I'll go with you instead.
- Where are the keys?

27
00:00:57,724 --> 00:00:58,600
- [groans]
- [squeals]

28
00:00:58,683 --> 00:01:01,227
[grunts and groans]

29
00:01:01,311 --> 00:01:03,146
[Audrey] <i>Thank you, Atoy.</i>

30
00:01:03,229 --> 00:01:05,231
[Willie] <i>Don't take a job</i>

31
00:01:05,315 --> 00:01:06,983
<i>that keeps you away too long.</i>

32
00:01:07,067 --> 00:01:09,819
Someone might hover around Cita.

33
00:01:09,903 --> 00:01:12,113
- Eh, she's old now! No one will--
- Go home!

34
00:01:12,197 --> 00:01:14,866
You don't even know, maybe Delfin
got to her behind your back.

35
00:01:14,949 --> 00:01:15,992
You're an asshole!

36
00:01:16,076 --> 00:01:17,577
- [bottle shatters]
- [groans]

37
00:01:17,660 --> 00:01:19,079
That's a bad joke!

38
00:01:19,162 --> 00:01:20,497
Run, you animal!

39
00:01:20,580 --> 00:01:23,958
You'll pick up your guts on the street!
[growls]

40
00:01:24,042 --> 00:01:27,629
I don't want my child to lose a father.

41
00:01:28,463 --> 00:01:29,798
[Atoy] Is that really the only reason?

42
00:01:29,881 --> 00:01:31,299
Or do you still want me?

43
00:01:31,382 --> 00:01:35,303
I'm not the same Elaine
you met on the island.

44
00:01:36,054 --> 00:01:37,847
Yes, I met other people.

45
00:01:39,974 --> 00:01:41,851
But I looked for you in all of them.

46
00:01:43,311 --> 00:01:44,771
[Atoy] <i>That's why none of them lasted.</i>

47
00:01:44,854 --> 00:01:48,858
PREVIOUSLY

48
00:01:48,942 --> 00:01:51,861
[suave music playing]

49
00:01:55,198 --> 00:01:57,242
- [Ibyang] Auntie Audrey?
- [gasps]

50
00:01:57,909 --> 00:02:00,453
- So many ants here.
- [Atoy] You're right.

51
00:02:00,537 --> 00:02:01,621
[Audrey] Ouch.

52
00:02:01,704 --> 00:02:03,081
[sneaky music playing]

53
00:02:03,164 --> 00:02:04,374
- Ouch.
- [quirky sting]

54
00:02:04,457 --> 00:02:06,668
Wait. What's that? What's that?

55
00:02:06,751 --> 00:02:07,836
- Hey.
- [clears throat]

56
00:02:09,546 --> 00:02:10,839
[quirky sting]

57
00:02:11,798 --> 00:02:14,467
Ibyang, what's going on?

58
00:02:16,136 --> 00:02:20,348
- I'm just a little hungry.
- [Atoy] Ahh.

59
00:02:20,431 --> 00:02:22,684
Do you want-- A sandwich?
Do you want to eat?

60
00:02:22,767 --> 00:02:24,102
Are you hungry?

61
00:02:24,185 --> 00:02:25,186
Mm-hmm.

62
00:02:27,397 --> 00:02:28,982
Did you kiss?

63
00:02:29,691 --> 00:02:31,609
- Ah-- No!
- Huh?

64
00:02:31,693 --> 00:02:32,527
What?

65
00:02:32,610 --> 00:02:33,778
- What are you saying?
- [Audrey] It's nothing.

66
00:02:33,862 --> 00:02:34,696
[titters]

67
00:02:34,779 --> 00:02:36,698
- You really--
- You're silly.

68
00:02:37,448 --> 00:02:41,161
Eh, because your lips look red.

69
00:02:41,244 --> 00:02:44,247
[Ibyang] And Auntie Audrey's
lipstick faded.

70
00:02:44,330 --> 00:02:45,707
Not really!

71
00:02:45,790 --> 00:02:47,584
There's still some, see.

72
00:02:47,667 --> 00:02:49,419
I just ate something, like…

73
00:02:49,502 --> 00:02:50,545
Ah, what was it?

74
00:02:50,628 --> 00:02:51,880
Annatto, yes.

75
00:02:51,963 --> 00:02:54,632
Maybe-- Oh, I just ate annatto earlier.

76
00:02:54,716 --> 00:02:55,675
[mutters]

77
00:02:55,758 --> 00:02:57,594
Annatto.

78
00:02:58,887 --> 00:02:59,804
Come on!

79
00:02:59,888 --> 00:03:01,222
Let's eat. Come on.

80
00:03:04,142 --> 00:03:05,226
[Atoy] Let's eat.

81
00:03:11,816 --> 00:03:13,234
[music fades]

82
00:03:13,318 --> 00:03:15,945
[suave theme music playing]

83
00:03:42,180 --> 00:03:46,017
Paldo, thank you so much
for your donation to the church.

84
00:03:46,601 --> 00:03:49,062
I can finally fix
the ceiling in the office.

85
00:03:51,272 --> 00:03:53,066
Father, it's nothing.

86
00:03:53,149 --> 00:03:56,236
Of course, I'm just making amends.

87
00:03:56,903 --> 00:03:58,529
Why are you making amends?
You have no sin to the church.

88
00:03:58,613 --> 00:04:00,698
[Noel] Willie, my friend,
let's talk about this!

89
00:04:00,782 --> 00:04:01,824
- [growls]
- Let's talk about this!

90
00:04:01,908 --> 00:04:03,826
[Willie] No friends here!

91
00:04:03,910 --> 00:04:06,996
- [growling]
- Help me. Help--Help me!

92
00:04:07,080 --> 00:04:08,373
Don't hide behind the priest!

93
00:04:08,456 --> 00:04:09,874
He won't save you from hell!

94
00:04:11,125 --> 00:04:12,252
[growling]

95
00:04:12,335 --> 00:04:13,461
[tense music playing]

96
00:04:13,544 --> 00:04:14,545
Willie, calm down!

97
00:04:14,629 --> 00:04:17,924
Ah, God calls us to mercy,
not to violence!

98
00:04:18,007 --> 00:04:20,468
Life is a sacred gift of God!

99
00:04:20,551 --> 00:04:23,429
Ah, Willie, put down that knife.
Put it down.

100
00:04:23,513 --> 00:04:25,390
Father, step aside,

101
00:04:25,473 --> 00:04:27,392
and just pray for him!

102
00:04:27,475 --> 00:04:31,854
[growling and groaning]

103
00:04:33,898 --> 00:04:35,525
As long as I'm chairman here,

104
00:04:35,608 --> 00:04:36,776
no one can stab anyone.

105
00:04:36,859 --> 00:04:37,819
Do you understand?

106
00:04:37,902 --> 00:04:38,820
- [Willie] Yes, Chairman.
- Answer!

107
00:04:38,903 --> 00:04:41,030
- Yes, Chairman.
- [man] Go on.

108
00:04:41,114 --> 00:04:42,824
You're an asshole, Willie!

109
00:04:42,907 --> 00:04:45,368
[grunting]

110
00:04:47,495 --> 00:04:48,496
Let me go.

111
00:04:48,579 --> 00:04:50,623
You know it's forbidden
to cause trouble here in Tabang Lupa.

112
00:04:50,707 --> 00:04:52,333
[music fades]

113
00:04:53,126 --> 00:04:54,335
Well, Paldo!

114
00:04:54,419 --> 00:04:56,170
Looks like you've changed.

115
00:04:56,254 --> 00:04:58,673
Before, you were the spark
of trouble here,

116
00:04:58,756 --> 00:04:59,924
but now, you're the one stopping it.

117
00:05:00,008 --> 00:05:01,426
Oh my, praise God!

118
00:05:01,509 --> 00:05:03,428
- [retches]
- [gasps, groans]

119
00:05:03,511 --> 00:05:05,013
What-- What's wrong?

120
00:05:05,096 --> 00:05:06,097
- What--
- Paldo!

121
00:05:06,180 --> 00:05:07,140
[laughs]

122
00:05:07,223 --> 00:05:08,099
[in English] The best!

123
00:05:08,182 --> 00:05:09,392
[in English] You're the best!

124
00:05:09,475 --> 00:05:10,643
Oh, you really are.

125
00:05:10,727 --> 00:05:11,477
- [laughs]
- [retches]

126
00:05:11,561 --> 00:05:13,146
Oh, God have mercy on you.

127
00:05:13,229 --> 00:05:14,188
Yes, Noel.

128
00:05:14,272 --> 00:05:16,691
Eh-- Stop drinking!

129
00:05:16,774 --> 00:05:18,318
Yes, Sir Noel. That's enough.

130
00:05:18,401 --> 00:05:20,445
Even I'll become
the cause of your trouble!

131
00:05:20,528 --> 00:05:21,487
- Go home now.
- [Cita] Noel!

132
00:05:21,571 --> 00:05:23,823
- [tense music playing]
- Oh no, you're in trouble.

133
00:05:23,906 --> 00:05:25,533
Noel, what's wrong with you?!

134
00:05:25,616 --> 00:05:27,201
You're so embarrassing!

135
00:05:27,285 --> 00:05:30,246
You even vomited on Father! Let's go home.

136
00:05:30,330 --> 00:05:31,581
- Did you make him drink?
- No.

137
00:05:31,664 --> 00:05:32,665
[Cita] Sorry.

138
00:05:32,749 --> 00:05:33,666
Come on! Let's go home--

139
00:05:33,750 --> 00:05:35,043
- Go home, Sir Noel.
- [Cita] You said you'd look

140
00:05:35,126 --> 00:05:36,127
- for work, but instead,
- Get some rest, get some rest.

141
00:05:36,210 --> 00:05:37,587
you just drank.

142
00:05:37,670 --> 00:05:38,713
You, you do nothing

143
00:05:38,796 --> 00:05:40,131
- but drink!
- Eh, I'll go home!

144
00:05:40,214 --> 00:05:41,966
- [Cita] You're so embarrassing!
- [Noel] Let's go home, let's go home!

145
00:05:42,050 --> 00:05:43,551
[rousing music playing]

146
00:05:43,634 --> 00:05:45,344
Wow, Mom, it stinks!

147
00:05:45,428 --> 00:05:48,389
[Noel] Of course, I vomited.

148
00:05:48,473 --> 00:05:51,059
[Cita] Get some water and a rag downstairs

149
00:05:51,142 --> 00:05:53,644
and make coffee for your father.

150
00:05:54,479 --> 00:05:55,521
Mom, we're leaving!

151
00:05:55,605 --> 00:05:57,482
We have basketball with T-Bak!

152
00:05:59,525 --> 00:06:01,402
- [Cita] Okay!
- Karla!

153
00:06:01,486 --> 00:06:03,696
Karla! Karla!

154
00:06:04,739 --> 00:06:07,283
It's late at night,
and you're still going out!

155
00:06:07,366 --> 00:06:09,285
Let her be!

156
00:06:09,869 --> 00:06:11,871
That's why her ego is so big.

157
00:06:14,707 --> 00:06:17,543
What-- What…

158
00:06:17,627 --> 00:06:20,713
did Willie say to you
that you suddenly hit him?

159
00:06:21,297 --> 00:06:22,632
He's annoying!

160
00:06:24,383 --> 00:06:26,511
You know, since you lost your job,

161
00:06:26,594 --> 00:06:27,804
- you've been a burden!
- Hey!

162
00:06:28,429 --> 00:06:31,390
Don't raise your voice at me, huh!

163
00:06:31,474 --> 00:06:33,810
Don't forget!

164
00:06:33,893 --> 00:06:35,520
I accepted you, huh!

165
00:06:35,603 --> 00:06:38,856
I accepted you
with all your shenanigans, huh!

166
00:06:38,940 --> 00:06:40,858
So, don't act all high and mighty with me!

167
00:06:40,942 --> 00:06:41,818
- Hmm?!
- Get your hands off me!

168
00:06:41,901 --> 00:06:43,820
- Don't act all high and mighty with me.
- [unsettling music playing]

169
00:06:43,903 --> 00:06:45,154
Do you know?

170
00:06:45,238 --> 00:06:47,657
Do you know what Willie told me?

171
00:06:48,157 --> 00:06:49,951
Why I got mad at him?

172
00:06:50,034 --> 00:06:54,455
My friend thinks Delfin stole you from me!

173
00:06:55,123 --> 00:06:57,792
It's true, isn't it?!
How many times did you do it, huh?!

174
00:06:57,875 --> 00:06:59,168
- How many times?!
- You're hurting me!

175
00:06:59,252 --> 00:07:00,878
You're hurting me!

176
00:07:00,962 --> 00:07:02,421
[growls]

177
00:07:02,505 --> 00:07:03,965
You're hurting me!

178
00:07:04,048 --> 00:07:05,883
Did you do it here in my own house?!

179
00:07:05,967 --> 00:07:07,635
Did you defile our bed?!

180
00:07:07,718 --> 00:07:09,554
No!

181
00:07:10,096 --> 00:07:11,347
No! Ah--

182
00:07:11,431 --> 00:07:13,266
- [heavy music playing]
- [groaning]

183
00:07:15,059 --> 00:07:17,854
He's been dead a long time!

184
00:07:17,937 --> 00:07:21,441
But until now, you still want him!

185
00:07:21,524 --> 00:07:23,860
Noel, you're the one who mentioned him!

186
00:07:24,527 --> 00:07:27,572
You're the one looking
for reasons to be angry at me!

187
00:07:28,114 --> 00:07:29,657
That's over!

188
00:07:29,740 --> 00:07:31,534
Whatever happened then, it's over!

189
00:07:31,617 --> 00:07:33,286
What-- What-- What do you mean over?!

190
00:07:33,369 --> 00:07:34,954
It happened!

191
00:07:35,037 --> 00:07:36,164
It's-- It's over!

192
00:07:36,247 --> 00:07:39,584
But the evidence is still there!

193
00:07:39,667 --> 00:07:41,419
I see it every day!

194
00:07:41,502 --> 00:07:44,005
Playing basketball!

195
00:07:44,088 --> 00:07:45,256
And a headache!

196
00:07:45,339 --> 00:07:46,841
[groans]

197
00:07:48,217 --> 00:07:52,763
[music swells]

198
00:07:59,812 --> 00:08:03,733
[music fades]

199
00:08:07,737 --> 00:08:08,779
Whoa.

200
00:08:09,489 --> 00:08:11,574
I was away for a short time.
That's almost gone!

201
00:08:16,787 --> 00:08:21,375
Tatoy, don't you have anything to tell me?

202
00:08:22,126 --> 00:08:24,504
Did something happen between you and…

203
00:08:24,587 --> 00:08:25,630
Auntie Audrey?

204
00:08:26,797 --> 00:08:28,424
- What happened? Psst. Hey, you.
- [quirky music playing]

205
00:08:28,508 --> 00:08:31,135
You're still very young.
What are you saying?

206
00:08:31,219 --> 00:08:33,387
What do you mean, "What happened?"

207
00:08:33,930 --> 00:08:35,848
I'm not a child anymore.

208
00:08:35,932 --> 00:08:37,767
And I get it.

209
00:08:38,684 --> 00:08:39,852
What do you mean you get it?

210
00:08:40,561 --> 00:08:41,646
It's bad to lie.

211
00:08:41,729 --> 00:08:43,523
But am I lying?

212
00:08:43,606 --> 00:08:44,774
[Ibyang] Hmm?

213
00:08:45,566 --> 00:08:49,695
Like when you said you ate annatto,
that's why your lips were red?

214
00:08:50,696 --> 00:08:55,034
Is there even an annatto tree
in this whole resort?

215
00:08:56,160 --> 00:08:59,163
And Auntie Audrey said
she was bitten by ants.

216
00:08:59,247 --> 00:09:00,831
But there were no ants there!

217
00:09:02,041 --> 00:09:04,794
[sneaky music playing]

218
00:09:06,963 --> 00:09:08,631
Did you get back together?

219
00:09:12,426 --> 00:09:14,887
- [sighs]
- Yiee!

220
00:09:15,972 --> 00:09:18,266
- [pleasant music playing]
- Your smile is different!

221
00:09:18,349 --> 00:09:19,684
Oh, oh!

222
00:09:20,560 --> 00:09:23,062
Tatoy is blushing, oh, oh.

223
00:09:23,854 --> 00:09:24,897
It's like this.

224
00:09:25,731 --> 00:09:27,024
We kissed.

225
00:09:27,775 --> 00:09:29,110
Yiee!

226
00:09:29,193 --> 00:09:30,069
- Yay!
- Oh, oh, psst.

227
00:09:30,152 --> 00:09:32,697
But we didn't get back together. Not yet.

228
00:09:32,780 --> 00:09:35,241
Anyway! Anyway, it's--
[in English] It's complicated.

229
00:09:35,324 --> 00:09:37,076
[in English] It's complicated.

230
00:09:37,159 --> 00:09:39,579
[pensive music playing]

231
00:09:39,662 --> 00:09:40,913
What are you doing here?

232
00:09:40,997 --> 00:09:42,582
I need to talk to Audrey.

233
00:09:42,665 --> 00:09:44,750
[smirks] What do you need from my sister?

234
00:09:51,424 --> 00:09:53,676
You adults!

235
00:09:53,759 --> 00:09:54,969
[music fades]

236
00:09:55,636 --> 00:09:57,555
The one older than me.

237
00:09:58,264 --> 00:09:59,265
Ahh.

238
00:09:59,348 --> 00:10:00,516
[Ibyang] You, guys.

239
00:10:00,600 --> 00:10:04,145
You even know "it's complicated".

240
00:10:04,812 --> 00:10:09,609
Were you happy
when you were with Auntie Audrey?

241
00:10:09,692 --> 00:10:10,693
Huh?

242
00:10:11,235 --> 00:10:14,739
And do you feel giddy
when you're with her?

243
00:10:15,615 --> 00:10:16,866
Eh…

244
00:10:16,949 --> 00:10:18,284
[Ibyang] And…

245
00:10:19,493 --> 00:10:21,746
you're not grumpy when she's around.

246
00:10:22,663 --> 00:10:24,957
All check, right? Uh?

247
00:10:25,916 --> 00:10:27,460
- [Ibyang] Huh?
- What do you think?

248
00:10:28,085 --> 00:10:29,503
What's your opinion?

249
00:10:30,046 --> 00:10:31,839
Hmm, yiee!

250
00:10:31,922 --> 00:10:33,633
Tatoy, oh!

251
00:10:33,716 --> 00:10:36,135
Don't let go of Auntie Audrey!

252
00:10:36,218 --> 00:10:37,345
[light music playing]

253
00:10:37,428 --> 00:10:41,098
It's like… a fairy tale come true.

254
00:10:42,224 --> 00:10:45,394
- Really?
- You broke up, then…

255
00:10:45,478 --> 00:10:47,688
- met again.
- Wow!

256
00:10:48,981 --> 00:10:51,025
Yiee! That's true love!

257
00:10:51,108 --> 00:10:53,694
I wish all had TL! Hmm.

258
00:10:53,778 --> 00:10:55,529
Hey, Tatoy, oh.

259
00:10:55,613 --> 00:10:56,947
- Tatoy, oh!
- [mutters]

260
00:10:57,031 --> 00:10:59,033
You even know "TL-TL."

261
00:10:59,116 --> 00:11:00,284
[Ibyang] Yiee, hmm.

262
00:11:01,202 --> 00:11:02,870
- How do you know that?
- Hmm?

263
00:11:02,953 --> 00:11:04,747
What are you watching?

264
00:11:07,333 --> 00:11:08,626
Good news, by the way.

265
00:11:09,794 --> 00:11:12,129
Tonet's brother
won't file charges anymore.

266
00:11:12,671 --> 00:11:14,715
Looks like they know
they don't have a case.

267
00:11:14,799 --> 00:11:16,300
[mysterious music playing]

268
00:11:16,384 --> 00:11:17,635
[in English] Great.

269
00:11:17,718 --> 00:11:19,387
But Atoy is really good, huh.

270
00:11:19,470 --> 00:11:22,723
After everything we did
to cover up what happened to Tonet,

271
00:11:22,807 --> 00:11:24,767
he still found evidence.

272
00:11:25,893 --> 00:11:26,811
[clicks tongue]

273
00:11:26,894 --> 00:11:29,146
I'm still not comfortable with that Atoy.

274
00:11:29,230 --> 00:11:30,731
[sighs]

275
00:11:30,815 --> 00:11:33,234
Audrey shouldn't have agreed
to co-parent with him.

276
00:11:33,901 --> 00:11:35,319
We can't do anything, hon.

277
00:11:35,403 --> 00:11:37,947
[in English] As long as they're
only doing co-parenting, we're…

278
00:11:38,030 --> 00:11:39,323
we're safe for now.

279
00:11:39,407 --> 00:11:40,533
[in English] You're not sure.

280
00:11:40,616 --> 00:11:43,327
Didn't you see how Audrey
defended that Atoy?

281
00:11:44,245 --> 00:11:45,621
What if they get back together?

282
00:11:45,704 --> 00:11:46,956
What if they get married?

283
00:11:47,540 --> 00:11:48,833
They can't get married.

284
00:11:48,916 --> 00:11:49,959
[Red, in English] Exactly.

285
00:11:50,876 --> 00:11:53,921
If they become husband and wife,
it's like letting a snake into the house.

286
00:11:54,004 --> 00:11:56,590
[suspicious music playing]

287
00:12:02,805 --> 00:12:04,598
[music fades]

288
00:12:06,142 --> 00:12:08,310
What are you doing here?

289
00:12:09,854 --> 00:12:10,938
Ah.

290
00:12:12,022 --> 00:12:13,357
Just getting some air.

291
00:12:13,983 --> 00:12:17,570
- [crickets chirping]
- [fire crackling]

292
00:12:17,653 --> 00:12:18,696
[in English] Same.

293
00:12:23,784 --> 00:12:25,244
Ibyang keeps pestering me.

294
00:12:26,662 --> 00:12:28,330
She knows what happened.

295
00:12:31,125 --> 00:12:32,209
[in English] About that.

296
00:12:35,212 --> 00:12:36,755
Why did you kiss me?

297
00:12:36,839 --> 00:12:39,341
[pensive music playing]

298
00:12:39,425 --> 00:12:42,845
[in English] If the kiss was just a kiss
and nothing more, then…

299
00:12:44,430 --> 00:12:45,848
Let's just forget it.

300
00:12:50,019 --> 00:12:51,687
It wasn't nothing to me.

301
00:12:51,770 --> 00:12:53,814
[light music playing]

302
00:12:53,898 --> 00:12:56,609
What about you? Was it nothing to you?

303
00:12:58,903 --> 00:13:01,030
[in English] I just want
to make sure that it was real.

304
00:13:02,072 --> 00:13:04,450
[in English] I don't want
to play games, Atoy.

305
00:13:06,494 --> 00:13:10,831
I want us to be whole for Janine.

306
00:13:11,832 --> 00:13:13,125
Me too.

307
00:13:14,960 --> 00:13:16,629
That's what I want too.

308
00:13:19,840 --> 00:13:21,759
I want us to get back together.

309
00:13:25,888 --> 00:13:27,223
But what about your family?

310
00:13:29,141 --> 00:13:30,226
What about Red?

311
00:13:30,309 --> 00:13:32,353
[scoffs] I don't care about him.

312
00:13:33,979 --> 00:13:35,272
This is our family.

313
00:13:35,981 --> 00:13:38,067
[mellow music playing]

314
00:13:40,736 --> 00:13:41,862
[in English] Can…

315
00:13:43,113 --> 00:13:44,990
[in English] Can we try to make this work?

316
00:13:48,202 --> 00:13:51,038
I hope we last
for more than just this night.

317
00:13:56,210 --> 00:13:57,586
I'm game for that.

318
00:14:01,131 --> 00:14:03,050
We'll do this right.

319
00:14:04,593 --> 00:14:06,345
For our family.

320
00:14:10,558 --> 00:14:13,185
I don't see anyone else with me but you.

321
00:14:18,649 --> 00:14:23,195
[sentimental music playing]

322
00:15:02,109 --> 00:15:03,736
[phone ringing]

323
00:15:04,945 --> 00:15:07,740
[in English] Ah, good morning, Dad!
Sorry, I just woke up, and…

324
00:15:08,574 --> 00:15:11,076
We've been here at the resort
since yesterday.

325
00:15:11,160 --> 00:15:13,120
How's your bonding with your daughter?

326
00:15:13,996 --> 00:15:15,581
Are you okay there at the resort?

327
00:15:16,498 --> 00:15:18,292
O-- We're fine here.

328
00:15:18,375 --> 00:15:19,209
[chuckles]

329
00:15:19,293 --> 00:15:21,545
Actually, can I talk to my granddaughter?

330
00:15:21,629 --> 00:15:23,589
I didn't greet her yesterday.

331
00:15:24,173 --> 00:15:25,341
Um…

332
00:15:26,675 --> 00:15:29,011
- Who are you talking to so early?
- Shh!

333
00:15:29,803 --> 00:15:30,971
Audrey?

334
00:15:31,055 --> 00:15:32,848
Do you have someone with you there?

335
00:15:32,932 --> 00:15:34,016
Oh, no, Dad!

336
00:15:34,099 --> 00:15:35,809
Janine is in the bathroom.

337
00:15:35,893 --> 00:15:38,354
Um, I'll just call you later, okay?

338
00:15:38,854 --> 00:15:40,064
[in English] No, no, no, no.

339
00:15:40,147 --> 00:15:43,275
Do you have a man
with you inside the room?

340
00:15:43,901 --> 00:15:44,985
No, Dad.

341
00:15:45,069 --> 00:15:47,529
[in English] Ah, I'll call you back later,
okay? Bye!

342
00:15:47,613 --> 00:15:50,199
- [phone blips]
- [suspicious music playing]

343
00:15:50,282 --> 00:15:54,578
You! My dad heard you! You're so noisy!

344
00:15:54,662 --> 00:15:55,496
Oh?

345
00:15:56,580 --> 00:15:59,124
Do you think your father will like me?

346
00:16:00,960 --> 00:16:01,961
[in English] I think so.

347
00:16:02,044 --> 00:16:04,588
[pensive music playing]

348
00:16:06,465 --> 00:16:08,509
- Oh, my God, sir, ma'am!
- [squeals]

349
00:16:08,592 --> 00:16:09,802
[staff, in English] Sorry to disturb you.

350
00:16:09,885 --> 00:16:12,179
But are you checked in?

351
00:16:12,262 --> 00:16:14,139
- Ah…
- No one is supposed to be here.

352
00:16:14,223 --> 00:16:17,434
Sorry, miss. We'll just pay
for the overnight stay.

353
00:16:17,518 --> 00:16:18,727
We have a honeymoon suite,

354
00:16:18,811 --> 00:16:21,188
if you want to continue
your romance there.

355
00:16:21,271 --> 00:16:23,649
Ah, is that so?
Okay, we'll just change clothes.

356
00:16:23,732 --> 00:16:24,900
Atoy!

357
00:16:24,984 --> 00:16:27,945
We came here for the kids,
not for a honeymoon!

358
00:16:28,028 --> 00:16:29,613
[sneaky music playing]

359
00:16:30,197 --> 00:16:32,741
Let's go, see them. Get dressed, quick!

360
00:16:33,325 --> 00:16:34,618
Ah, I'll sleep first.

361
00:16:40,082 --> 00:16:41,250
[music fades]

362
00:16:43,585 --> 00:16:44,586
Ah, they're here.

363
00:16:46,463 --> 00:16:49,800
- Ah, dear, we'll get food for you.
- [Janine] Okay.

364
00:16:49,883 --> 00:16:51,301
Oh, what do you want?

365
00:16:51,385 --> 00:16:52,553
What do you want to eat?

366
00:16:53,345 --> 00:16:55,973
[Ibyang] All the dishes and eggs!

367
00:16:56,056 --> 00:16:58,434
- All? Are you sure?
- Yes.

368
00:16:58,517 --> 00:17:00,894
[muffled chattering in the distance]

369
00:17:04,773 --> 00:17:05,941
Ibyang.

370
00:17:06,734 --> 00:17:09,194
You can't sit here. Find another table.

371
00:17:09,278 --> 00:17:11,905
Eh, the other tables are full.

372
00:17:11,989 --> 00:17:14,491
If the other tables are full,

373
00:17:14,575 --> 00:17:16,201
then eat in the room instead.

374
00:17:16,285 --> 00:17:18,996
I just want our family at this table.

375
00:17:20,039 --> 00:17:21,165
There.

376
00:17:21,790 --> 00:17:24,460
But I want to be with Tatoy here.

377
00:17:25,085 --> 00:17:27,087
And it's not your birthday anymore.

378
00:17:27,171 --> 00:17:29,798
So, your birthday rules don't apply to me.

379
00:17:29,882 --> 00:17:31,091
I just want to eat.

380
00:17:31,175 --> 00:17:34,219
[rousing music playing]

381
00:17:34,303 --> 00:17:36,722
[chair scraping, then utensils shattering]

382
00:17:38,015 --> 00:17:39,600
- [gasps]
- Hey.

383
00:17:42,978 --> 00:17:44,772
Are you okay? What happened?

384
00:17:44,855 --> 00:17:45,856
Come here.

385
00:17:45,939 --> 00:17:46,899
[groans]

386
00:17:52,905 --> 00:17:55,324
Are you okay?
What? Where-- Where does it hurt?

387
00:17:55,407 --> 00:17:58,285
Huh? Move your foot like this, like this.

388
00:17:58,368 --> 00:18:00,412
Now the plates are broken.

389
00:18:00,496 --> 00:18:01,663
You have to pay for that!

390
00:18:01,747 --> 00:18:03,373
It's your fault.

391
00:18:03,874 --> 00:18:07,002
You pulled the chair
just as I was about to sit.

392
00:18:07,086 --> 00:18:08,087
No, I didn't.

393
00:18:08,170 --> 00:18:10,798
So, it's my fault? It's all you!

394
00:18:11,465 --> 00:18:12,341
So, what?

395
00:18:12,424 --> 00:18:14,635
The chair moved on its own?

396
00:18:15,594 --> 00:18:16,595
Don't blame me, Janine.

397
00:18:16,678 --> 00:18:17,930
[in English] Don't me.

398
00:18:18,013 --> 00:18:20,224
- [Ibyang, in English] Don't me!
- Don't shout at me!

399
00:18:20,307 --> 00:18:22,893
You're not invited here.
You're not part of the family!

400
00:18:22,976 --> 00:18:23,977
Psst, Janine.

401
00:18:24,061 --> 00:18:26,855
[music swells]

402
00:18:27,439 --> 00:18:29,650
Your attitude is still bad.

403
00:18:29,733 --> 00:18:31,860
I gave you a chance on your birthday, huh!

404
00:18:32,486 --> 00:18:33,570
You better leave.

405
00:18:33,654 --> 00:18:35,322
- Hey.
- [in English] Janine, stop it!

406
00:18:35,405 --> 00:18:37,449
Come with me! [sighs]

407
00:18:37,533 --> 00:18:39,493
[Audrey] Come on! [sighs]

408
00:18:40,160 --> 00:18:42,246
- [tense music playing]
- What happened?

409
00:18:42,329 --> 00:18:43,580
Why are you fighting again?

410
00:18:44,540 --> 00:18:46,750
Sir, I saw it.

411
00:18:46,834 --> 00:18:50,754
The other girl pulled her seat,
that's why she fell.

412
00:18:52,256 --> 00:18:53,882
Okay, thank you.

413
00:19:00,180 --> 00:19:01,431
Yesterday you and Ibyang were okay.

414
00:19:01,515 --> 00:19:02,850
Why are you fighting again?

415
00:19:02,933 --> 00:19:04,434
She started it!

416
00:19:04,518 --> 00:19:07,729
And why is it that Daddy
always sides with Ibyang?!

417
00:19:07,813 --> 00:19:10,274
My dear, he's not siding with Ibyang!

418
00:19:10,357 --> 00:19:12,651
He didn't say you were wrong!

419
00:19:12,734 --> 00:19:13,652
Even so, Mommy.

420
00:19:13,735 --> 00:19:16,113
I just want the two of you
to be with me on this vacation,

421
00:19:16,196 --> 00:19:17,281
but I'm annoyed

422
00:19:17,364 --> 00:19:19,324
because Daddy still takes care of Ibyang!

423
00:19:19,992 --> 00:19:21,743
[pensive music playing]

424
00:19:21,827 --> 00:19:23,453
And now he wants to adopt her!

425
00:19:24,788 --> 00:19:29,126
Dear, that's why we want
you two to get along.

426
00:19:29,710 --> 00:19:31,503
Mommy, no way.

427
00:19:31,587 --> 00:19:33,338
Tell Daddy not to adopt Ibyang

428
00:19:33,422 --> 00:19:35,883
because that means
we'll always be together!

429
00:19:35,966 --> 00:19:37,259
I really don't like Ibyang, Mommy.

430
00:19:37,342 --> 00:19:40,345
We'll never be friends.
We'll always fight!

431
00:19:41,096 --> 00:19:43,056
[in English] Janine, please.

432
00:19:43,140 --> 00:19:44,183
[sighs]

433
00:19:44,266 --> 00:19:45,225
[in English] Mommy.

434
00:19:46,560 --> 00:19:49,062
Why does he have to adopt Ibyang?

435
00:19:49,938 --> 00:19:53,150
We don't need Ibyang in the family
because I'm already here!

436
00:19:53,817 --> 00:19:56,278
Am I not enough as Daddy's child?

437
00:19:56,361 --> 00:19:58,113
Doesn't he love me?!

438
00:19:58,197 --> 00:20:01,366
[heavy music playing]

439
00:20:15,464 --> 00:20:16,340
[sobs]

440
00:20:18,675 --> 00:20:20,928
[Noel] Cita! Come on, eat now!

441
00:20:21,011 --> 00:20:22,304
Stop acting up.

442
00:20:22,387 --> 00:20:24,264
[Cita] I'll just finish this.

443
00:20:25,140 --> 00:20:26,391
[Karla] Hey.

444
00:20:29,061 --> 00:20:30,646
All of this food is mine!

445
00:20:31,855 --> 00:20:36,777
If you want, cook your own or buy outside!

446
00:20:37,736 --> 00:20:39,780
Noel, that's too much!

447
00:20:41,156 --> 00:20:42,741
That food's all mine!

448
00:20:43,617 --> 00:20:45,244
[pensive music playing]

449
00:20:45,994 --> 00:20:47,871
I'll just eat at Brother Atoy's place.

450
00:20:49,539 --> 00:20:50,999
What are you mumbling there?

451
00:20:51,083 --> 00:20:52,584
Do you want me to choke?!

452
00:20:53,460 --> 00:20:54,586
No!

453
00:20:54,670 --> 00:20:58,090
I said I'll just eat
at Brother Atoy's place.

454
00:20:58,173 --> 00:21:00,717
At least there, no one
will forbid me from eating.

455
00:21:01,301 --> 00:21:02,219
Well then!

456
00:21:02,302 --> 00:21:04,096
Eat there. Don't come back!

457
00:21:09,434 --> 00:21:10,811
Enough!

458
00:21:13,063 --> 00:21:15,607
If you don't want to eat,
then I'll eat it all.

459
00:21:18,360 --> 00:21:22,781
Tatoy, aren't you going to scold Janine?

460
00:21:22,864 --> 00:21:24,241
You heard it.

461
00:21:24,324 --> 00:21:26,910
Someone saw her pull my chair.

462
00:21:27,953 --> 00:21:29,496
I don't want bad vibes.

463
00:21:29,579 --> 00:21:31,748
I don't want our vacation to be ruined.

464
00:21:31,832 --> 00:21:33,250
[sighs]

465
00:21:33,333 --> 00:21:34,376
Ibyang…

466
00:21:35,294 --> 00:21:37,671
Don't-- Don't trigger Janine anymore.

467
00:21:37,754 --> 00:21:40,048
I'll talk to her another day.

468
00:21:40,132 --> 00:21:42,092
Okay? I don't want bad vibes.

469
00:21:42,175 --> 00:21:43,635
- Um, so…
- Okay.

470
00:21:43,719 --> 00:21:46,096
- [Ibyang] I'll try.
- [in English] Are we all good?

471
00:21:46,847 --> 00:21:50,684
Janine, let's just forget
what happened, okay?

472
00:21:50,767 --> 00:21:52,602
Let's just enjoy.

473
00:21:52,686 --> 00:21:54,021
- Let's go fishing.
- Yes.

474
00:21:54,104 --> 00:21:55,981
- Uh, Tatoy.
- [Atoy] Hmm?

475
00:21:56,064 --> 00:21:58,066
I'll just go to the bathroom.

476
00:21:58,150 --> 00:22:00,569
I'll follow later for fishing.

477
00:22:00,652 --> 00:22:02,237
Ah, I'll pee too, Mommy.

478
00:22:02,321 --> 00:22:04,489
- [Audrey] Ah, I'll go with you.
- No need.

479
00:22:05,991 --> 00:22:07,534
Ibyang is here.

480
00:22:07,617 --> 00:22:09,453
Promise, we won't fight.

481
00:22:10,078 --> 00:22:11,747
- Promise, huh.
- [Janine] Yes.

482
00:22:13,623 --> 00:22:16,793
Um, Ibyang, the bathroom
in the lobby is broken.

483
00:22:16,877 --> 00:22:20,464
- But I know another bathroom.
- Okay.

484
00:22:32,768 --> 00:22:36,772
Janine, is there really a bathroom here?

485
00:22:36,855 --> 00:22:38,231
[sighs] There is.

486
00:22:38,315 --> 00:22:39,816
Just follow me.

487
00:22:40,650 --> 00:22:41,777
Fine.

488
00:22:43,403 --> 00:22:44,654
Where is it?

489
00:22:45,614 --> 00:22:50,869
[suspicious music playing]

490
00:22:52,079 --> 00:22:53,163
What's that?

491
00:22:55,499 --> 00:22:57,501
This really belonged to Sister Tonet.

492
00:22:58,043 --> 00:22:59,795
I just took it…

493
00:23:00,545 --> 00:23:03,173
so I could always be with her.

494
00:23:03,757 --> 00:23:06,134
Ahh. Let me see, hmm.

495
00:23:06,760 --> 00:23:08,220
Hey, Janine!

496
00:23:08,720 --> 00:23:10,138
That's mine!

497
00:23:13,100 --> 00:23:14,518
- Ibyang.
- Mmm.

498
00:23:14,601 --> 00:23:15,977
Don't-- Hey!

499
00:23:16,061 --> 00:23:17,771
[cackles]

500
00:23:19,648 --> 00:23:20,690
They're taking so long.

501
00:23:20,774 --> 00:23:22,067
Exactly.

502
00:23:25,529 --> 00:23:28,323
Have you told Janine about us?

503
00:23:29,282 --> 00:23:30,700
Not yet.

504
00:23:31,326 --> 00:23:34,913
I wanted us to tell them together.

505
00:23:35,747 --> 00:23:39,292
But Janine is still upset with you.

506
00:23:40,293 --> 00:23:43,046
I don't know how we'll tell her.

507
00:23:43,130 --> 00:23:44,881
[suspicious music playing]

508
00:23:44,965 --> 00:23:46,800
Janine!

509
00:23:47,384 --> 00:23:48,802
You said we wouldn't fight anymore,

510
00:23:48,885 --> 00:23:51,304
but you're still making me angry!

511
00:23:51,388 --> 00:23:53,098
Do whatever you want! [cackles]

512
00:23:53,765 --> 00:23:54,641
Hey.

513
00:23:54,724 --> 00:23:57,394
[tense music playing]

514
00:24:03,024 --> 00:24:04,901
[Ibyang grunts]

515
00:24:22,752 --> 00:24:25,130
Okay, that's it.

516
00:24:26,298 --> 00:24:27,382
[sighs]

517
00:24:27,465 --> 00:24:28,842
[cackles]

518
00:24:28,925 --> 00:24:30,218
That's what happens.

519
00:24:33,680 --> 00:24:35,932
- [thuds softly]
- [groans]

520
00:24:36,016 --> 00:24:37,267
Ouchy.

521
00:24:38,018 --> 00:24:39,311
[sighs]

522
00:24:44,816 --> 00:24:46,568
- [foreboding music playing]
- [hissing]

523
00:24:46,651 --> 00:24:48,236
[squeals]

524
00:24:50,572 --> 00:24:53,783
[tense music playing]

525
00:24:58,622 --> 00:25:02,375
You should thank me
because I accepted this child,

526
00:25:02,459 --> 00:25:05,170
even though she's not mine!

527
00:25:05,253 --> 00:25:06,838
Tell her the truth!

528
00:25:06,922 --> 00:25:08,757
Delfin is your father!

529
00:25:08,840 --> 00:25:10,091
Atoy is your brother!

530
00:25:10,175 --> 00:25:11,176
‪UP NEXT

531
00:25:11,259 --> 00:25:13,511
Because as long as Ibyang is here,

532
00:25:13,595 --> 00:25:17,933
she'll always feel
that she's not enough for us.

533
00:25:18,016 --> 00:25:22,062
Atoy, this isn't
a shallow insecurity that…

534
00:25:22,145 --> 00:25:24,940
will just disappear when she grows up.

535
00:25:25,607 --> 00:25:27,150
So, what do you want me to do now?

536
00:25:27,234 --> 00:25:28,860
[Atoy] I'm sorry, Ibyang.

537
00:25:28,944 --> 00:25:31,238
This is hard for me too, but…

538
00:25:31,321 --> 00:25:33,990
to keep you from fighting with Janine…

539
00:25:34,950 --> 00:25:37,077
You're not going to adopt me anymore?

540
00:25:37,160 --> 00:25:38,828
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

541
00:25:38,912 --> 00:25:40,997
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

542
00:25:41,081 --> 00:25:44,084
♪ <i>One cut, and it's settled</i> ♪

543
00:25:44,167 --> 00:25:46,419
Subtitle translation by: Rachel C. Arias
